  <main_text>
    <l n="1">succedunt ascendentibus.</l>
    <l n="2" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="3" para="true">Quanam legitime dicantur haereditates?</l>
    <l n="4" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="5" para="true">Spurii matri succedunt.</l>
    <l n="6" para="true">§. 4.</l>
    <l n="7" para="true">Jus adcrescendi obtinet in successione</l>
    <l n="8">ab intestato.</l>
    <l n="9" type="heading" level="1" caput="5" para="true">LIBR.3. INSTIT. TIT. 5.</l>
    <l n="10" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De Successione cognatorum.</l>
    <l n="11" para="true">In Princ.</l>
    <l n="12" para="true">1. OLim cognati quandoque admit-</l>
    <l n="13">terentur.</l>
    <l n="14" para="true">2. Quinam sint cognati?</l>
    <l n="15" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="16" para="true">Ad quem usque gradum succedatur?</l>
    <l n="17" type="heading" level="1" caput="6" para="true">LIBR. 3. INSTIT. TIT. 6.</l>
    <l n="18" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De Gradibus cognationum.</l>
    <l n="19" para="true">In Princ.</l>
    <l n="20" para="true">1. CUr graduum cognitio si necessaria?</l>
    <l n="21" para="true">2. Affinium non sunt gradus.</l>
    <l n="22" para="true">3. Definitur quid sit stipes, quid linea,</l>
    <l n="23">&amp; quotuplex.</l>
    <l n="24" para="true">4. Gradus explicatur.</l>
    <l n="25" para="true">§. 9.</l>
    <l n="26" para="true">1. Oculis plus credimus quam auribus.</l>
    <l n="27" para="true">2. Jus Canonum explicatur, &amp; notatur.</l>
    <l n="28" type="heading" level="1" caput="7" para="true">LIBR. 3. INSTIT. TIT.7.</l>
    <l n="29" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De Servili cognatione.</l>
    <l n="30" type="foot" para="true">[Right column text, from "LIBR.3. INSTIT. TIT.8." onward, follows in part 2.]</l>
    <l n="31">
      <i>Aliter ex l. Papiâ succedit patronus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="32" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="33" para="true">
      <i>Aliter succedit patronus jure Justinia-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="34">
      <i>neo. Differentia notantur inter ingenuorum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="35">
      <i>&amp; libertorum successiones.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="36" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 4.</l>
    <l n="37" para="true">
      <i>Summa Largiani Senatusconsulti</i>
    </l>
    <l n="38">
      <i>pro- ponitur.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="39" type="heading" level="1" caput="9" para="true">LIBR. 3. TIT. 9.</l>
    <l n="40" type="heading" level="1" caput="9">De Assignatione libertorum.</l>
    <l n="41" type="heading" level="2" para="true">In Princ.</l>
    <l n="42" para="true">
      <i>Assignatio quid sit, &amp; quo jure</i>
    </l>
    <l n="43">
      <i>introducta?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="44">
      <i>An cui assignatur libertus, eum suo</i>
    </l>
    <l n="45">
      <i>filio possit assignare?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="46" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="47" para="true">
      <i>Nepoti recte fit assignatio.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="48" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="49" para="true">
      <i>An emancipato possit assignari?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="50" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="51" para="true">
      <i>Quomodo fiat assignatio?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="52" type="heading" level="1" caput="10" para="true">LIBR. 3. INSTIT. TIT. 10.</l>
    <l n="53" type="heading" level="1" caput="10">De bonor. Possessionibus.</l>
    <l n="54" type="heading" level="2" para="true">In Princ.</l>
    <l n="55" para="true">
      <i>Definitur bonorum possessio. Quo sensu prator emendet jus civile? Possi-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="56" para="true">Servorum non est cognatio, vel successio. Quid jure Canonum?</l>
